  "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes #59970. The five DSV4.1-specific sparse metadata builders declare `AttentionCGSupport.ALWAYS`, so with `cudagraph_mode=FULL_AND_PIECEWISE` prefill and mixed batches get FULL-graph captured even though their prefill metadata is not graph-safe, and the engine dies with an illegal memory access once adaptive verification runs mixed batches at concurrency. Downgrade them to `UNIFORM_BATCH` and report the speculation width as the varlen decode bound, mirroring the reviewed pattern from #59751.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Prefill and mixed batches leave FULL capture for all five builders named in #59970: `DeepseekV4FlashMLAMetadataBuilder`, `DeepseekV4FlashInferSparseMLAMetadataBuilder`, `DeepseekSparseSWAFlashInferMetadataBuilder`, `DeepseekSparseSWAFlashMLAMetadataBuilder`, `CompressorMetadataBuilder`. `FlashMLAMegaAttnBackend` inherits the same builder, so it is covered too.\n- FULL varlen decode graphs are kept for uniform batches sized up to 1 + num_speculative_tokens, so DSpark adaptive verification keeps its decode graphs.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/worker/test_attn_utils.py -q\n```\n\n82 passed on CPU. The 10 new parametrized cases pin, per backend and num_speculative_tokens in {0, 7}, that support resolves to `UNIFORM_BATCH`, that decode widths up to the speculation width stay graph-eligible, and that one token wider is rejected with the reported bound. Changed-file pre-commit (ruff-check, ruff-format) passed.\n\nNot run: the B300 (SM103) end-to-end reproducer from the issue, no compatible hardware available here, and CI does not exercise these builders. The change only narrows what FULL graphs capture: prefill moves to the piecewise path that the issue's adaptive-verification-off and FULL_DECODE_ONLY arms already exercise for 30+ minutes under load, so no batch that was not captured before becomes captured.\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause, from the issue's arm table: adaptive verification on + FULL_AND_PIECEWISE hits the IMA 4/4 within a minute; verification off in the same mode is stable; verification on with FULL_DECODE_ONLY is stable. The failing ingredient is prefill inside FULL graphs. Each affected builder now also overrides `get_varlen_cudagraph_max_query_len` to return `max_decode_query_len(vllm_config)` (1 + num_speculative_tokens on MRV2), the same width the V2 runner uses when it builds varlen decode replays.\n\nNot a duplicate of #59751: that PR changes only the generic `FlashInferMLASparseTRTLLMMetadataBuilder` for #59681, while the DSV4.1 model wires its own five builders, which the #59970 reporter calls out explicitly. Checked the issue thread and open PRs referencing #59970 before starting; nothing else covers them.\n\nAI assistance: Kimi Code (Kimi K3) prepared the patch and tests; I reviewed every changed line and ran the validation above.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n\n",
